  "coverage": {
    "acsEstimateStatus": "Every U.S. county and Puerto Rico municipio has its ACS 2020-2024 B23001 age rows in resident-employment-counties.json (3,222 rows, read from the key-free static table). A county absent from it (Guam, the U.S. Virgin Islands, American Samoa and the Northern Mariana Islands have no ACS five-year table) still uses the explicit tunable proxy.",
    "nationalApplicability": "National civilian noninstitutional age-cohort proxy does not establish local or territorial employment. Population-to-workplace and source-vintage application remain estimates.",
    "olderAgeDenominator": "B23001 age 65+ has no distinct Armed Forces subtotal. Those observed rates use total age residents, not a claimed civilian-only denominator. Younger civilian totals subtract the actually reported sex-specific Armed Forces estimates."
  },
  "countyInputContract": "countyCounts[GEOID][ageRow.id] must contain valid source estimate strings civilianPopulation and employed. civilianPopulation is the pooled-sex age total minus the table reported armed-forces subtotal. Missing/suppressed cells are not zero; omit them and expose fallback. Older bins have no armed-forces branch in B23001. Metadata alone supplies no population/employed counts."
